{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1012086-killing-an-ananasi","id":1012086,"title":"Killing an Ananasi","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-04T11:46:07-08:00","id":1012086,"title":"Killing an Ananasi","content":"Question for experienced Ananasi players and STs-<br /> What happens when an Ananasi is taken beyond incapacitated? I understand how their healing works and all that, but I'm not seeing anything in their breedbook mirroring how Garou, or even vampires, handle &quot;death&quot; by mundane weapons.<br /> <br /> Can someone seriously, theoretically, kill one with a single well-placed bullet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:19:09-08:00","id":1012101,"title":"","content":"Personally I'd let a incapacitated Anasasi burn blood to heal damage reflexively, and if they were out of blood...I'd probably treat it similar to a human healing from incapacitated...but that's just me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:04:10-08:00","id":1012158,"title":"","content":"It also depends on if they are in Crawling form. If a single master spider survives, which is likely if you are not using area effect weapons, they can just eat other spiders until they recover enough mass to become Ananasi again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:42:24-08:00","id":1012188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1012086-killing-an-ananasi?p=1012101#post1012101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'd let a incapacitated Anasasi burn blood to heal damage reflexively, and if they were out of blood...I'd probably treat it similar to a human healing from incapacitated...but that's just me</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see this, though it isn't completely necessary. I don't mind it going either way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1012086-killing-an-ananasi#post1012086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone seriously, theoretically, kill one with a single well-placed bullet?</div> </div> </div> </div>If an Ananasi is prepared they are near unkillable. If taken by surprise, they can be killed at least somewhat easily. So yes, in theory by RAW it's possible.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T15:40:13-08:00","id":1012214,"title":"","content":"Though they do soak lethal damage, so you will likely not get a second shot if the first does not kill them (you would probably have to do around 18 dice of damage for a guaranteed kill, which is difficult).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T16:08:15-08:00","id":1012238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1012086-killing-an-ananasi?p=1012214#post1012214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though they do soak lethal damage, so you will likely not get a second shot if the first does not kill them (you would probably have to do around 18 dice of damage for a guaranteed kill, which is difficult).</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on breed maybe. I seem to remember a debate on whether or not Changers could soak lethal in their breed forms. This may or may not be an edition thing as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T01:46:39-08:00","id":1012451,"title":"","content":"Their Queen is a secretive one...remember that the biology of an Ananasi is actually not entirely human. Its human form has hidden pedipalps. Given this, in my chronicle (now a year or two old) an Ananasi in any form converts to Crawlerling reflexively when incapacitated. This can be avoidied by spending Blood reflexively instead. This tweak has worked very nicely so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T07:50:29-08:00","id":1012575,"title":"","content":"Well, if they were born a spider, that would be their breed form, so it is appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T12:43:41-08:00","id":1012722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1012086-killing-an-ananasi?p=1012575#post1012575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if they were born a spider, that would be their breed form, so it is appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't explicitly stated. I don't know whether or not Crawlerling form is actually considered a spider born Ananasi's breed form. Honestly, I was always under the impression that Pithas becomes the default breed form for spider born. But looking back through books (quickly, so I very well may have missed it), I can't find any place where it says anything one way or the other.<br /> <br /> If anyone finds a definitive statement on this, I'd welcome citation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T13:18:35-08:00","id":1012745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1012086-killing-an-ananasi?p=1012188#post1012188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an Ananasi is prepared they are near unkillable. If taken by surprise, they can be killed at least somewhat easily. So yes, in theory by RAW it's possible.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:04:49-08:00","id":1012764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1012086-killing-an-ananasi?p=1012745#post1012745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Could you elaborate on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW, they don't have a means to save themselves from going below incap (like Garou's Rage roll to recover or a Vampire's torpor state). So a lucky shot does have a chance of killing them. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> pointed out, doing 18 dice of damage is a pretty good guarantee, but just getting lucky can do it.<br /> <br /> If they're prepared though, they can spend Blood (reflexively) to fast shift to Crawlerling, possibly even in instead of a defensive (dodge or parry) action. And in Crawlerling, if at least 1 Leader survives, the Ananasi will (most probably) reform in a few days to a few weeks. Killing 150+ lbs of spiders in 1 go is usually pretty impossible, especially since attackers aren't generally aware of how Ananasi meta-physiology works. So any smart Ananasi (and they generally should be) won't put itself in a position that it can't survive. It is even arguable that they can spend willpower to mixed morph a leader away from the main homid body (which they might do anytime entering into a possibly fatal situation).<br /> <br /> There are also some useful merits that can greater aid this sort of strategy but since merits are things most individuals don't have access to, they aren't worth specifically planning around or for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 12-05-2016, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:13:24-08:00","id":1012770,"title":"","content":"Ananasi Crawlerling form isn't a typical Breed form, as it can be adapted by eating different species of arachnid. Likewise, the Homid form with its pedipalps, etc. Given this and the lack of anything saying otherwise, I always assumed they actually don't have a Breed form as its commonly understood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:19:12-08:00","id":1012773,"title":"","content":"In my campaigns, I required my Ananasi characters to trade one of their beginning Gifts from the Hive Mind Merit, so it has been ubiquitous in my campaigns in the past. I also gave them Human Form and one of Emotional Attachments or Empathy for 'free', as it made the campaigns easier. Everything balanced out to '0' freebie points, so my players did not complain when I informed them about the benefits.<br /> <br /> Ananasi with Hive Mind are nearly impossible to kill in Crawlernig form, as every spider is effectively a leader. If one spider survives (out of an average 70,000 spiders formed from a 70 kilogram Ananasi), they will come back to take their revenge. It is a great Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:29:44-08:00","id":1012776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1012086-killing-an-ananasi?p=1012770#post1012770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ananasi Crawlerling form isn't a typical Breed form, as it can be adapted by eating different species of arachnid. Likewise, the Homid form with its pedipalps, etc. Given this and the lack of anything saying otherwise, I always assumed they actually don't have a Breed form as its commonly understood.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what form do you have spider born revert to if knocked unconscious? I think that's the situation that is most likely to come up, where a Changer is forced into a specific form.<br /> <br /> I think I had always assumed it was Pithus because the description (from memory) for spider born said that they have to keep eating until the reach the mass of the Pithus. The spider grows and grows until that time. They don't multiply out, so it never occurred to me (until this thread) to consider Crawlerling as a possible &quot;breed form&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T22:07:34-08:00","id":1013002,"title":"","content":"A sniper hitting Anasasi in the head is probably going to kill one. They're more vulnerable in that respect than some other supernatural beings are. On the other hand they don't have to worry about Frenzy the way werewolves and vampires do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T08:23:05-08:00","id":1013176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1012086-killing-an-ananasi?p=1012776#post1012776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what form do you have spider born revert to if knocked unconscious?</div> </div> </div> </div>I go with Crawlerling, as I said, but I don't consider that reverting to a Breed form. That's because my character is arachnid born, and started out in a bunch of bananas as a Brazilian wandering spider. Per the text in CB20 &quot;They must literally eat their way to a body mass that can accommodate their change in form&quot;. So as far as the menu was concerned, Pithus form was actually attained pretty late, with Homid and Crawlerling form being reached about the same time (since Crawlerling form breaks down into individuals of equal mass). And it was agreed that this was the form the character would revert to, because it was the least inconspicuous and supernatural form. However, WHAT he actually breaks down into is now part of what he must decide, since in munching his way through the Amazon he consumed large numbers of other, smaller spiders. If he was reverting to a Breed form, it would be as <i><b>Phoneutria Fera</b></i>, but he doesn't have to do that anymore, so it makes no sense to categorise it as his Breed form. And as I said earlier, I think Ananasa (the creatrix of this form, don't forget) is really big on making sure her secrets don't get out, and this is the only form that makes sense for that.<br /> Since he is a floor dwelling predator and was born without the need or form to build webs, he also had to acquire that ability by eating webmakers, btw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 12-06-2016, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T12:34:00-08:00","id":1013326,"title":"","content":"Well, the 'breed' form of an arachnid born has to be either Pithus or Crawlerling and, since Pithus causes Delirium, the fact that there are not news stories about two hundred pound spiders (complete with videos at 6 pm!) suggests that the 'breed' form should be Crawlerling. Humans can rationalize a stranger being 'eaten' by a horde of spiders (they even ate his bones!) much easier than they could rationalize a two hundred pound terror spider (gibber, whimper, screaming panic into the streets, etc). As an ST, I would rule that I control the Crawlerling form while the character is Incapacitated, and its instinct would be to hide and to heal.<br /> <br /> I am sort of curious though, since the species of spiders change as the Ananasi absorb other spiders, do Ananasi just spiritual adopt local spiders into their Crawlerling form when they want to bread with the local spider population? Is reproduction with the local spider population something that just happens when they submerge for a few years into the local spider population or do they have to make a conscious choice to reproduce? And how many female spiders within the Crawlerling form of a female homid Ananasi have to be fertilized to make a homid Ananasi pregnant when they reform?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T01:36:15-08:00","id":1013644,"title":"","content":"Pithus being a breed form is something that I really don't see... imagine all the giant spider corpses that you didn't manage to hide :P<br /> <br /> All the shifters have a Breed, if they have a breed they have a default breed form. For Ananasi it's just that their form evolves a bit from the birth baseline. So they can be killed by a high damage attack they cannot react to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T07:43:35-08:00","id":1013757,"title":"","content":"Of course, unconscious homid Ananasi are sort of hard to hide. That is why I required Ananasi characters in my games to take Human Form [3] and one of either Empathy [-3] or Emotional Attachment [-3], to minimize the potential complications of being Ananasi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T09:36:04-08:00","id":1013803,"title":"","content":"Eh. Ananasa herself takes a much closer hand in her children than most any of the Incarna patrons. So the one time its come up in game (an Ananasi dying), I just had their body calcified into the Gauntlet by pattern spiders.<br /> This was an easy explanation for why the Ananasi, one of the most populous Changing Breeds, were thought extinct (or near enough to it). <br /> <br /> And I can certainly see the argument for Crawlerling being their effective breed form, and will go ahead and use that is it ever comes up again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}